{
  "presses": ["L-index-bottom-in", "R-index-bottom-in", "R-pinky-top", "L-index-home-in"],
  "note": "T3: pressed anchors {L-index-bottom-in,R-index-bottom-in,R-pinky-top} + L-pinky-bottom => {B,C,F,S}. Rotation after: {L-index-home-in,L-pinky-bottom,L-ring-bottom} (so next letter on L-index-home-in/L-pinky-bottom/L-ring-bottom changed). T4: press same 3 anchors + L-index-home-in. T5: same anchors + L-ring-bottom. Then intersect (T4set ∩ T5set) to get the 3 anchor letters; remaining element is 4th-key letter each time."
}

{
  "presses": [
    "L-index-bottom-in",
    "R-index-bottom-in",
    "R-pinky-top",
    "L-ring-bottom"
  ],
  "note": "Use anchors A={L-index-bottom-in,R-index-bottom-in,R-pinky-top}. T4 (A + L-index-home-in) produced set {B,C,F,G}. Now do T5 = A + L-ring-bottom. Then anchorLetters=intersection(T4set,T5set); the remaining element in each set is the 4th-key letter (so T5 remaining = L-ring-bottom). Last rotation after T4: {L-index-top,R-index-home,R-ring-top} (not in A)."
}

{
  "presses": [
    "L-index-home",
    "L-ring-bottom",
    "L-middle-top",
    "L-middle-bottom"
  ],
  "note": "T11: L-middle-bottom=Q; L-ring-bottom=K; L-middle-top=S. Remaining: L-index-home and L-index-home-in are {G,O} in some order. Next chord [L-index-home, L-ring-bottom(K), L-middle-top(S), L-middle-bottom(Q)] => symbol on L-index-home is the remaining one (G or O)."
}

{
  "presses": [
    "L-index-bottom-in",
    "L-ring-bottom",
    "L-middle-top",
    "L-middle-bottom"
  ],
  "note": "Known: L-index-home=O; L-index-home-in=G; L-middle-top=S; L-middle-bottom=Q; L-ring-bottom=K. Next press: [L-index-bottom-in, L-ring-bottom, L-middle-top, L-middle-bottom]. Expect letters {K,Q,S, x} => L-index-bottom-in=x (if no rotation affecting these keys)."
}

{
  "presses": [
    "L-index-bottom",
    "L-index-home",
    "L-middle-top",
    "L-middle-bottom"
  ],
  "note": "Known: L-index-home=O; L-index-home-in=G; L-index-bottom-in=F; L-middle-top=S; L-middle-bottom=Q; L-ring-bottom=K. Next: press [L-index-bottom, L-index-home, L-middle-top, L-middle-bottom]. If no rotation among these 4, returned symbols are {O,S,Q,x} => L-index-bottom=x."
}

{
  "presses": ["L-index-bottom", "L-middle-bottom", "L-middle-top", "L-ring-top"],
  "note": "Known: L-index-home=O; L-index-home-in=G; L-index-bottom-in=F; L-index-bottom=H; L-middle-top=S; L-middle-bottom=Q; L-ring-bottom=K. T14 press [L-index-bottom,L-middle-bottom,L-middle-top,L-ring-top]. If next obs shows none of these 4 rotated, then L-ring-top=(returned symbol not in {H,Q,S}). Next (if L-ring-top known): press [L-ring-home, L-ring-bottom, L-middle-top, L-ring-top] to deduce L-ring-home."
}

{
  "presses": ["L-ring-home", "L-ring-bottom", "L-middle-top", "L-ring-top"],
  "locks": {
    "L-ring-top": "E"
  },
  "note": "T16: after [L-ring-home,L-ring-bottom,L-middle-top,L-ring-top] expect symbols {K,S,E,X}. Using rotation notice: if none rotated -> L-ring-home=X. If rotations include L-ring-home among these 4, then map X to the key position that ends up holding the remaining unknown; use rotated-keys list to place X."
}

{
  "presses": ["L-ring-home", "L-ring-top", "L-ring-bottom", "L-pinky-top"],
  "note": "We learned L-ring-home=J (from set {J,L,R,U} with no rot; intersects prior {E,J,K,S}). Remaining: {L-ring-top,L-ring-bottom,L-middle-top} = {E,K,S}; {L-pinky-top,L-index-top,R-index-home-in}={L,R,U}. Next: press {L-ring-home,L-ring-top,L-ring-bottom,L-pinky-top} so output has J + two of {E,K,S} (ring-top/bottom) + one of {L,R,U} (pinky-top). Then compare with T18 planned {L-ring-home,L-ring-top,L-middle-top,L-index-top} to assign each key."
}

{
  "presses": [
    "L-ring-home",
    "L-ring-top",
    "L-middle-top",
    "L-index-top"
  ],
  "note": "From T18 (no rot): L-ring-home=J; L-pinky-top=L; {L-ring-top,L-ring-bottom}={E,K} => L-middle-top=S. Also earlier {L-pinky-top,L-index-top,R-index-home-in}={L,R,U} => L-index-top in {R,U} and R-index-home-in is the other. T19 chord {L-ring-home,L-ring-top,L-middle-top,L-index-top} should yield {J,S,(E/K),(R/U)}; use output+rotation notice to fix L-ring-top (E vs K) and L-index-top (R vs U), then deduce L-ring-bottom and R-index-home-in."
}

{
  "presses": ["L-ring-top", "L-ring-home", "L-middle-top", "L-pinky-home"],
  "locks": {
    "L-pinky-top": "L",
    "L-ring-home": "J",
    "L-ring-top": "E",
    "L-middle-top": "S",
    "L-index-top": "U",
    "L-ring-bottom": "K",
    "R-index-home-in": "R"
  },
  "note": "New from T19(no rot): L-ring-top=E; L-index-top=U; R-index-home-in=R; L-ring-bottom=K. Also have L-pinky-top=L, L-ring-home=J, L-middle-top=S. T19 press next: [L-ring-top(E),L-ring-home(J),L-middle-top(S),L-pinky-home(?)] => L-pinky-home is the 4th symbol from returned set."
}
